cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Math Lab: an agent-driven library of attempted approaches to open conjectures"
message: >-
  If you use this library, please cite it. Note that every record was written
  and reviewed by AI agents and has not been peer-reviewed by a human
  mathematician; cite it as a record of attempted approaches, not as a source
  of established results.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Walker
    given-names: Joe
repository-code: "https://github.com/Joe975/math-lab"
abstract: >-
  A library of attempted approaches to seven open mathematical conjectures
  (union-closed sets/Frankl, Erdos-Gyarfas, Erdos-Straus, Singmaster, lonely
  runner, graceful trees, Collatz), produced by an autonomous agent loop with
  adversarial verification. Records dead ends as first-class output alongside
  verified computational results, and separates published background from the
  lab's own findings so that later attempts can be made either blind or
  informed.
keywords:
  - open conjectures
  - automated mathematical research
  - AI agents
  - union-closed sets conjecture
  - negative results
license: MIT
